; A posting that fails to parse reports only its own line ("While parsing
; posting:"), never the enclosing automated, periodic or regular
; transaction, and parsing continues with the next entry.  parse_post()
; signals failure only by throwing; it never returns a null posting.
; The automated transaction has a check line and a valid posting before
; the bad one, so its context flag has already been set once.
; A line that begins with '^' ends the file: the malformed entry after
; it is never read.

= /Food/
    check amount > 0
    (Budget:Food)    1
    (Budget:Food)    (1 +)

~ Monthly
    Expenses:Rent    $500 @@
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/01 Grocer
    Expenses:Food    $10.00 @ @ $2
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Cafe
    Expenses:Food    $5.00
    Assets:Cash

^ The parser stops here.
2024/01/03 Never read
    Expenses:Food    $1.00 @ @ $2
    Assets:Cash

test bal -> 3
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 13:
While parsing posting:
  (Budget:Food)    (1 +)
                   ^^^^^
Error: ) operator not followed by argument
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
While parsing posting:
      Expenses:Rent    $500 @@
                       ^^^^^^^
Error: Expected a cost amount
While parsing file "$FILE", line 20:
While parsing posting:
  Expenses:Food    $10.00 @ @ $2
                            ^^^^
Error: No quantity specified for amount
end test
